-- title:
--   The q-adic place is centred at a good point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. the image of $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let `ResidueField A` be the residue field of $A$ and let $W$ be a finite set of places of the characteristic-$q$ modular function field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of Laurent series over `ResidueField A` generated by the $j$-series `jqModC` and its $M'$-fold $q$-substitution `jqNModC`) over `ResidueField A`; the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, that is, the places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator lying in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)` (the set of $j$ for which every elliptic curve with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point). Here a place of $F$ over $K$ is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $\top$ and a principal ideal ring; `ord` denotes the associated order of vanishing and `evalAt` the value in $K$ of a regular element at a rational place. Let `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` be the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, and `fieldBar q M'` the geometric level field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ with $H=$ `levelH q M'`, the kernel of the reduction map of unit groups attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`; the hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   The reduction data are: a `ConstantReduction` $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, i.e. a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, the conditions that a constant lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when it lies in $A$, that `R₀.residue` is compatible with reduction of constants, that every nonzero element has a constant multiple in `R₀.integers` with nonzero residue, that `R₀.placeMap` preserves degrees of places, and that `R₀.placeMap` carries the divisor of an element with nonzero residue to the divisor of its residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀.residue`, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Fix a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb Z/q$, and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ of valuation subrings of `fieldBar q M'` indexed by $W$. The Igusa hypotheses are: `hIg_inf`, which describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as the Gauss ring, $f$ belonging to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f\cdot\bar y=\bar x$ (bars denoting coefficientwise inclusion $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$); `hIg`, which provides for every $\ell$ in the projective line some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with `redQ q γ • lineInfty q = ℓ` and $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj`, the injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and `hIg_perm`, which says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ the pullbacks of the $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permute the family, via some permutation $\sigma$ of the projective line.
--
--   The supersingular hypotheses are: `hSS_A`, that a constant from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when it lies in $A$; `hSS_over`, which for $s\in W$ and $f\in$ `R₀.integers` whose order is non-negative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the base-changed $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has non-negative order, and whose `R₀.residue` lies in the valuation subring of $s$, asserts that the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and that for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue of $f$, the difference of $f$ and the constant $a$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and in its maximal ideal; `hSS_fix`, that $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for every $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hSS_tr`, that each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ contains an element $t$ such that $t$ minus any constant from $A$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ and is a unit there.
--
--   Further data: a `RegularProlongation` $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` (a valuation subring `R.integers` with a surjective residue map onto the latter field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, with every nonzero element having a constant multiple of nonzero residue), with `hR` identifying `R.integers` with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$; and `hR₀O`, that an element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   The arithmetic hypotheses on the base are: an element $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the pullback of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is henselian local, and has algebraically closed residue field, and such that (`hκ`) every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$; a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; and a finite extension $K_1$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ together with a valuation subring $A_1$ of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (that is, $x\in A_1$ iff $x\in A$), assumed to be a henselian discrete valuation ring. The field `fieldBar q M'` is regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   Under these hypotheses, the following holds for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`; $F_0$ is stable under every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; $F_0$ is regular over $k_0$ in the sense that for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, a relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$; and every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, i.e. has rational coefficients, belongs to $F_0$.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum inside `fieldBar q M'` of the image of $K_1$ and $F_0$ over $k_0$. The statement is then further quantified over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is required to agree with the inclusions $A_1\subseteq K_1\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`, and over a nonzero element $j_1\in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the base-changed $j$-expansion `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` viewed in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` through `hle`.
--
--   Let $\mathfrak X_1=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A₁ T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgInf` (those integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$) along the middle chart, with structural morphisms `ιFin`, `ιInf` into $\mathfrak X_1$ and `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$. Three predicates are introduced. `InStalk x f`, for a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ and $f\in T_1$, says that for every point $y$ of the finite chart with `ιFin` sending $y$ to $x$ there are $g,h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h\notin y$ and $f\cdot h=g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for every point of the infinite chart over $x$ with `chartAlgInf`. `InMax x f` is the same statement with the extra requirement $g\in y$ in both charts. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational (the structure map $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to P.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective) and that every $f\in T_1$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$, and satisfies: the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $<1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. Finally `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of five clauses: `toBase` sends $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; $x$ specialises only to itself; for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every element of `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$; the same for the infinite chart with `chartAlgInf`; and for every point $y$ of the finite chart over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ does not lie in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7).
--
--   The conclusion asserts the existence of a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ whose valuation subring is `qIntegersBar (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) (fieldBar q M')`, the subring of elements whose Laurent series has non-negative order, and of a point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_1$ such that `GoodPt x` and `Centred P x` hold.
--
--   This is the cusp clause in the construction of the smooth Igusa base model: it exhibits the $q$-adic place of the geometric level field — the cusp $\infty$, whose valuation ring records the order of vanishing of the $q$-expansion — as centred at a closed point of the special fibre of the two-chart integral model that lies on the $\infty$-Igusa branch and away from supersingular $j$-invariants. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_igusaBaseModel_smoothPointStalks), where the residue discs of the reduction are taken to be the sets of places centred at such points.
